"YqJdfBkUD3PahL7\",\"output_index\":0,\"sequence_number\":103,\"summary_index\":0}\n\nevent: response.reasoning_summary_text.done\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.reasoning_summary_text.done\",\"item_id\":\"rs_02d71b7a964e1c6e016af13c4fd6d887d095970e238836b46c\",\"output_index\":0,\"sequence_number\":104,\"summary_index\":0,\"text\":\"**Determining time zones**\\n\\nI need to figure out the timezone because I can't just guess the system's timezone based on the user. The date offset isn’t IANA standard. I could list absolute times for tomorrow’s local date, but guessing the zone is risky. If I can retrieve the system timezone, I might read from /etc/localtime for that info. It could be better to establish a broad window for events, like listing from Nov 9 to Nov 11 in UTC, then refine based on the event's timezone.\"}\n\nevent: response.reasoning_summary_part.done\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.reasoning_summary_part.done\",\"item_id\":\"rs_02d71b7a964e1c6e016af13c4fd6d887d095970e238836b46c\",\"output_index\":0,\"part\":{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Determining time zones**\\n\\nI need to figure out the timezone because I can't just guess the system's timezone based on the user. The date offset isn’t IANA standard. I could list absolute times for tomorrow’s local date, but guessing the zone is risky. If I can retrieve the system timezone, I might read from /etc/localtime for that info. It could be better to establish a broad window for events, like listing from Nov 9 to Nov 11 in UTC, then refine based on the event's timezone.\"},\"sequence_number\":105,\"summary_index\":0}\n\nevent: response.output_item.done\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.output_item.done\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"rs_02d71b7a964e1c6e016af13c4fd6d887d095970e238836b46c\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABq8TxUJaFrGUFeCjHs9sjAPg-YhgwHMKPdBc_mfTdcGiqu-xWz5QYUxNx4llaJuxt-l0x40baKW4mmMWKB9-YKsxnh3HmafI0yxn8bGSKKCdxnCICPxg5qkp-9REryijACZ4_PIp5rzpN51K-Mq4HUGNxz1Mqn-8_xHnqpJce_dY